          <div style="flex: 1;">
            <h3 style="color: #007acc; font-size: 16pt; margin-top: 0;">Project Summary</h3>
            <ul style="font-size: 12pt; line-height: 1.7; margin-top: 8pt;">
              <li>Successfully demonstrated core Computer Graphics principles: surface normals, cross products, (M<sup>-1</sup>)<sup>T</sup> normal matrices, and dot products.</li>
              <li>Built a fully working, standalone Blender 5.0.1 application (<code>Industrial_Surface_Inspection.blend</code>).</li>
              <li>100% verified sum invariance across all viewing directions.</li>
              <li>Real-time 15.49 ms cycle time with zero viewport slowdown.</li>
            </ul>
          </div>
          <div style="flex: 1; background: #f8fafc; border: 1pt solid #cbd5e1; border-radius: 8pt; padding: 16pt;">
            <h3 style="color: #007acc; font-size: 16pt; margin-top: 0;">Future Scope</h3>
            <ol style="font-size: 12pt; line-height: 1.7; margin-top: 8pt;">
              <li><strong>Raycast BVH Self-Occlusion:</strong> Combine normal orientation with raycasting to detect geometric shadowing behind flanges.</li>
              <li><strong>360° Automated Turntable Replay:</strong> Automated scan sequence recording cumulative surface visibility.</li>
              <li><strong>Continuous False-Color Heatmaps:</strong> EEVEE thermal shaders showing continuous 0.0 to 1.0 gradients.</li>
            </ol>
          </div>
        </div>
